@page "/about"
@layout MainLayout

<div class="login-wrapper">
    <div class="about">
        <h1 class="about-header">Greetings Adventurer</h1>

        <div class="about-body">
            My name is Joey Guynes, the head coder for Legends of the Lance. Back in the day (90s) this was a project that I did. Back then it was a lovelly MUD that
            I coded for. It was how I spent a good ammount of my time that wasn't playing Magic the Gathering or Dungeons and Dragons. It was a way for me to express
            my creativity without being burdened by the "Real World". Many years after it depreciated, I wanted to renew it, but thinking like a true nerd, I needed
            to update it at the same time.
            <br /><br />
            Legends of the Lance was originallly based on Dragonlance by Margert Weis and Tracy Hickman. Now with this itteration, it is no longer tied to that world.
            It is a fully emmersive fantasy world that is all it's own.
        </div>
        <div class="about-body">
            I want to take a moment to thank those who helped design this game:
            <ul>
                <li>Joey Guynes - Lead Coder</li>
                <li>Charles Gabriel. Commissioned by OpenGameArt.org (http://opengameart.org) - Sprites and Animation</li>
                <li>Juhani Junkala. https://opengameart.org/content/5-chiptunes-action - Background Music</li>
                <li>cynicmusic.com & pixelsphere.org - Alternate Music</li>
                <li>Jon K. Fite - Vicotry Music</li>
                <li>https://opengameart.org/content/rpg-sound-pack - Sound Effects</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>